---
import '../styles/watermark.css';

const lastUpdated = 'July 18, 2026';
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
		<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
		<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
		<meta name="robots" content="index,follow" />
		<title>Privacy Policy — Pixel Freedom</title>
		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
		<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
	</head>
	<body>
		<main>
			<header class="page-header">
				<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
				<p>Pixel Freedom — Chrome extension</p>
				<p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
			</header>

			<article class="prose">
				<section>
					<h2>The short version</h2>
					<p>
						Pixel Freedom does not collect, store, transmit, or sell any of your
						data. There are no accounts, no analytics, no trackers, and no servers.
						Every photo you open is processed entirely on your own device, inside
						your browser. Nothing you load into the extension ever leaves your
						computer.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>What the extension does</h2>
					<p>
						Pixel Freedom is a photo tool that opens as a sidebar over the page
						you're browsing. It lets you crop, resize, convert the format of, and
						strip the metadata from an image so the file you download comes out
						clean. All of this — the image decoding, editing, metadata reading and
						removal, and re-encoding — runs locally in your browser using
						WebAssembly. No image or edit is uploaded anywhere.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>Data we collect</h2>
					<p><strong>None.</strong> Specifically, Pixel Freedom does not collect or process:</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Personal or identifying information</li>
						<li>The images you open, edit, or download</li>
						<li>Metadata read from your images (EXIF, C2PA, etc.)</li>
						<li>Your browsing history or the content of pages you visit</li>
						<li>Location, IP address, or device identifiers</li>
						<li>Usage analytics or telemetry of any kind</li>
					</ul>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>How your images are handled</h2>
					<p>
						When you drop a file into the sidebar, or drag an image off the page
						you're viewing, that image is held only in your browser's memory for
						the duration of your editing session. It is passed to local, in-browser
						code to be edited and re-encoded, and is discarded when you close the
						sidebar or leave the page. It is never sent to us or any third party.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>Permissions and why they're needed</h2>
					<p>
						Chrome requires the extension to declare certain permissions. Here is
						exactly how each one is used:
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li>
							<strong>activeTab &amp; scripting</strong> — used to open the sidebar
							on the current page only when you click the toolbar icon. Nothing runs
							on any page until you explicitly invoke it.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>Host access (http/https pages)</strong> — used solely to fetch
							an image you deliberately drag into the sidebar from the page you're
							browsing. It is not used for any background access to page content, and
							the extension does not read, monitor, or transmit the pages you visit.
						</li>
					</ul>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>Third parties</h2>
					<p>
						Pixel Freedom does not include any third-party analytics, advertising,
						or tracking libraries, and it does not share data with anyone —
						because it does not collect any data to share.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>Children's privacy</h2>
					<p>
						Because Pixel Freedom collects no data at all, it collects no data from
						children. The extension is safe for users of any age in this respect.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
					<p>
						If this policy ever changes, the updated version will be posted on this
						page with a new "Last updated" date. Continued use of the extension
						after a change constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>Contact</h2>
					<p>
						Questions about this policy or the extension's privacy practices can be
						sent to
						<a href="mailto:contact@pixelfreedom.xyz">contact@pixelfreedom.xyz</a>.
					</p>
				</section>
			</article>

			<footer class="page-footer">
				<a href="/">← Back to Pixel Freedom</a>
			</footer>
		</main>

		<style is:global>
			main {
				max-width: 760px;
				margin: 0 auto;
				padding: 3rem 1.25rem 5rem;
			}

			.page-header {
				text-align: center;
				margin: 0 auto 2.5rem;
			}

			.page-header h1 {
				font-size: 2.5rem;
				font-weight: 600;
				letter-spacing: -0.03em;
				margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
				background: linear-gradient(135deg, #fff 0%, #a5b4fc 100%);
				-webkit-background-clip: text;
				background-clip: text;
				-webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
			}

			.page-header p {
				color: var(--text-muted);
				font-size: 1.0625rem;
				margin: 0;
			}

			.page-header .updated {
				font-size: 0.875rem;
				margin-top: 0.5rem;
			}

			.prose section {
				margin-bottom: 2rem;
			}

			.prose h2 {
				font-size: 1.25rem;
				font-weight: 600;
				letter-spacing: -0.02em;
				color: var(--text-main);
				margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
			}

			.prose p {
				color: var(--text-muted);
				font-size: 1rem;
				line-height: 1.65;
				margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
			}

			.prose ul {
				margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
				padding-left: 1.25rem;
				color: var(--text-muted);
				line-height: 1.65;
			}

			.prose li {
				margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
			}

			.prose strong {
				color: var(--text-main);
			}

			.prose a {
				color: #a5b4fc;
				text-decoration: none;
			}

			.prose a:hover {
				text-decoration: underline;
			}

			.page-footer {
				margin-top: 3rem;
				padding-top: 1.5rem;
				border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);
				text-align: center;
			}

			.page-footer a {
				color: var(--text-muted);
				font-size: 0.9375rem;
				text-decoration: none;
			}

			.page-footer a:hover {
				color: var(--text-main);
			}
		</style>
	</body>
</html>
